\pard\plain\qc\sb120\sa80\b\fs20 Figure 5.2: Mean return on 10,000 test tasks (longer bar is better).\par
\pard\plain\qj\sl360\slmult1\sa100\fi720\fs24 The DDQN earns +0.189, 9.3% above the best rule and 24% above the single agent, with a higher success rate than the single agent (0.47 against 0.34) at a cost of 0.215 against 0.123, which the reward judges worth paying. The fixed pipeline pays 0.293 for almost no gain. The 9.3% is just under the 10% bar set at the start, and both numbers are reported. Paired with the rule on identical tasks, every seed is ahead by +0.009 to +0.022, each beyond its 95% interval (about 0.007). The advantage is small in absolute terms (about 0.016 per task). The policy always solves first, stops or tidies after a passed check, retries after a failed one and gives up early on hard tasks, a structure it found without being told.\par
