\pard\plain\qc\sb120\sa80\b\fs20 Figure 5.3: Return in six worlds for the fixed rule and the DDQN, both trained or tuned once.\par
\pard\plain\qj\sl360\slmult1\sa100\fi720\fs24 The fixed rule breaks in the research-heavy world (+0.029, below the single agent at +0.067). The DDQN keeps +0.077, level with the retuned rule at +0.072, without retuning. It is at or above the retuned rule in five of six worlds and loses only under tight budgets (+0.167 against +0.172, within noise); that range partly overlaps training, and the retuned rule used only 2,000 tuning tasks. The value of the DDQN is robustness more than peak return.\par
