\pard\pagebb\s1\outlinelevel0\keepn\sb240\sa120\ql\plain\b\fs32 APPENDIX A: CODE ORGANISATION\par
\pard\plain\qj\sl360\slmult1\sa100\fi720\fs24 The repository has six code packages: {\b env} (simulator and Gym-style environment with action masks), {\b baselines} (single agent, fixed pipeline, rule routers), {\b rl} (Double DQN, replay buffer, training loop), {\b eval} (evaluation runner and the tuning, shift, ablation, blind and real-trace studies), {\b llm} (model client, the four agents, the 50 tasks with graders, the trace-cache builder and replay environment) and {\b app} (race engine, charts and the Streamlit dashboard). The folder {\b docs} holds the decision log, the specification, the demonstration runbook and the logs of every reported run; {\b tests} holds 87 automated tests covering reward loopholes, graders, replay, the race engine and the dashboard.\par
\pard\s1\outlinelevel0\keepn\sb240\sa120\ql\plain\b\fs32 APPENDIX B: REPRODUCING THE RESULTS\par
\pard\plain\qj\sl360\slmult1\sa100\fi720\fs24 From the repository root, with Python 3 and PyTorch installed: run the tests with {\b PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m pytest -q tests}. Run the main comparison and tuning with {\b python3 -m eval.tune_dqn}, the shift study with {\b python3 -m eval.shift}, the ablations with {\b python3 -m eval.ablate} and {\b python3 -m eval.ablate_blind}, and the real-trace studies with {\b python3 -m eval.real_eval runs/cache_qwen3b.jsonl} and the same command for {\b runs/cache_gptoss20b.jsonl}, followed by {\b python3 -m eval.real_eval_typed} with the cache path. The dashboard starts with {\b ./run_demo.sh}. Logs of every run reported here are in {\b docs/logs}.\par
